  no Upsilon moves a, because Upsilon enters only through x, i.e. only through I_e.  Lowering Upsilon buys b tilt but at
  the price of a stellar M/L below anything a stellar population gives for an old red galaxy, and it never touches a.
  aperture R_e/8 : framework a = 1.095, b = -0.835   (the aperture moves the zero point, not the tilt)
  aperture R_e/2 : framework a = 1.095, b = -0.819   (the aperture moves the zero point, not the tilt)
  aperture R_e   : framework a = 1.094, b = -0.805   (the aperture moves the zero point, not the tilt)

