4.  K-BAND CROSS-CHECK
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  K band, N = 7949: observed a = 0.771, b = -0.713; framework a = 1.108, b = -0.834; virial a = 1.109, b = -0.850; framework noiseless a = 2.0021
  [PASS] 52.6 the K band says the same thing as the J band, so the verdict is not a photometric-band artefact: the framework's sigma coefficient is again pinned to the virial value while the data's is far below it   (framework K-band a = 2.0021 noiseless (theorem holds) and 1.108 noisy, against a virial 1.109 and an observed 0.771)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
MUTATION CONTROLS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  [PASS] M1 mutation: with a_0 divided by 100 every galaxy is Newtonian and the framework's plane must collapse onto the exact virial plane -- it does, so the b tilt reported above really is the kernel's doing and not an artefact of the Jeans solve   (a_0/100 gives noiseless (a, b) = (2.0000, -1.0000) against the virial (2.0000, -1.0000) and the framework's (2.0024, -0.9656))
  [PASS] M2 mutation: shuffling which galaxy's predicted dispersion goes with which galaxy's radius and surface brightness must destroy the plane -- it does   (shuffled (a, b) = (-0.008, -0.686) against the framework's (+1.095, -0.835))

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
VERDICT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  noiseless coefficients -- virial (2.000, -1.000); framework (2.002, -0.966); non-homology (1.662, -0.946); observed, de-attenuated (1.403, -0.734)
  Sanders' 2000 proposal rested on ellipticals sitting AT the MOND transition.  Measured on 6dFGS with a stellar-population
  M/L of 1.2, the median internal acceleration at R_e is x = 17 a_0 (5-95%: 6 to 40) -- an order of
  magnitude above the transition, where Route A's exponential return has almost nothing left to give: the median boost is
  1.5% in dynamical mass.  The proposal fails on the data, not on the algebra.
  What survives, and it is worth keeping: the SIGN and the STRUCTURE are the framework's.  The observed mass-to-light residual
  really is keyed to surface brightness rather than to luminosity, which is what a_0 predicts and what a mass-dependent dark
  fraction does not; the framework simply supplies a minority of its size.  The item is recorded as a LIABILITY on amplitude
  with a structural point in the framework's favour, and the 'tilt within 0.05' bar is NOT met.

